  "caveats": [
    "HONESTY FRAME: hashing char-trigram embedder (D-005) measures lexical overlap, not semantic faithfulness; absolute numbers are modest and NOT the paper's claim.",
    "entail_fn is a cosine surrogate, not a real NLI model (D-002 open); SE=0 (no generate_fn wired), so CHRS = lambda*H_cascade exactly.",
    "Trace construction gives zero upstream risk: s1 echoes its only document (H=0) and s2 has no retrieved context (H undefined -> 0 in the cascade), so H_cascade(s3) == H(s3) and the pipeline-aware pathway adds NO signal on this slice. The head-to-head validates the harness and thresholding, not the paper's cascade-amplification advantage.",
    "H on this slice partially confounds answer LENGTH with hallucination: gold answers are short entities while hallucinated answers are sentences, which inflates the H gap under a lexical embedder.",
    "Sample-scale: 150 of 10,000 records (106 tuning / 44 held-out); wide confidence intervals, numbers are provisional.",
    "kappa comes from calibration on synthetic-clean CHRS, not this dataset's clean traces; per-lambda thresholding is fixed rather than recalibrated."
  ]
